---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Dujiangyan Panda Base Visit Guide - Tips & What to Expect"
  description="Complete visit guide for Dujiangyan Panda Base: what to bring, best viewing spots, itinerary suggestions, and insider tips for a great panda experience."
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-accent-600 uppercase mb-3">Visit Guide</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-warm-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">
      Your Complete Visit Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-warm-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      What to bring, where to go, and how to make the most of your time at Dujiangyan Panda Base.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 p-4 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>⚠ Currently closed:</strong> Dujiangyan Panda Base has been closed since April 23, 2026 for renovations. This guide is preserved for reference. <a href="/closure-updates" class="underline font-medium">See current alternatives →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-warm-500">Last updated: July 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 md:pb-24 space-y-16">
    <div>
      <SectionHeader title="What to bring" subtitle="The base is on a hillside with limited facilities inside. Bring these essentials for a comfortable visit." />
      <div class="mt-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {["Comfortable walking shoes -- the base is on a hillside with uneven paths", "Sunscreen and a hat -- limited shade in some open areas", "Water and snacks -- limited food options inside the base", "Camera with a zoom lens -- pandas can be at a distance from viewing areas", "Passport -- required for ticket purchase and entry for foreign visitors", "Rain jacket or umbrella -- Sichuan weather is unpredictable year-round"].map((item) => (
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> {item}</div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-warm-600">
        Not sure what to wear for the volunteer program specifically? See our <a href="/volunteer-program/#faq" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">volunteer FAQ</a> for clothing requirements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader title="Best viewing times" subtitle="Pandas follow a predictable daily rhythm. Plan around it." />
      <div class="mt-6 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-green-200 bg-green-50/50">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-800">8:30 - 10:30 AM</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-warm-600">Best time. Pandas are eating breakfast and most active. This is when you will see them climbing, playing, and munching bamboo.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-yellow-200 bg-yellow-50/50">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-yellow-800">11:00 AM - 1:30 PM</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-warm-600">Nap time. Most pandas sleep after their morning meal. Good time for the museum, gift shop, or a walk on the nature trails.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-green-200 bg-green-50/50">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-800">2:00 - 4:30 PM</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-warm-600">Second activity window. Pandas wake up for an afternoon snack and sometimes play. Quieter than morning, with softer light for photos.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader title="Suggested half-day itinerary" />
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-3">
        {[
          { time: "8:30 AM", desc: "Arrive when gates open. Pandas are most active during morning feeding." },
          { time: "9:00 AM", desc: "Visit the main panda enclosures. Watch pandas eat bamboo and play." },
          { time: "10:30 AM", desc: "Walk the nature trails to see pandas in the hillside enclosures." },
          { time: "12:00 PM", desc: "Lunch break. Bring your own or visit nearby restaurants in Dujiangyan." },
          { time: "1:30 PM", desc: "Visit the panda museum and learn about conservation efforts." },
          { time: "2:30 PM", desc: "Final walk through the base. Gift shop for panda souvenirs." },
          { time: "3:30 PM", desc: "Head back to Chengdu or continue to nearby attractions. The <a href='/nearby-attractions' class='text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline'>Dujiangyan Irrigation System</a> is just 15 minutes away." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="flex gap-4 p-3 rounded-lg bg-warm-50 border border-warm-100">
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-600 w-20 shrink-0">{item.time}</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-warm-700" set:html={item.desc} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <SectionHeader title="Insider tips" />
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500">+</span> Weekdays are significantly quieter than weekends -- aim for Tuesday to Thursday if possible</li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500">+</span> Pandas nap midday -- plan your visit for early morning or late afternoon</li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500">+</span> Combine with Dujiangyan Irrigation System (UNESCO) -- just 15 minutes away</li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500">+</span> No flash photography -- it stresses the pandas and is strictly enforced</li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm text-warm-700"><span class="text-accent-500">+</span> Plan around the <a href="/best-time-to-visit" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">seasons</a> -- spring and autumn offer the best weather and most active pandas</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
